  {
   "tag": "Brass",
   "h2": "Buzz the Lips",
   "body_html": "<p><strong>Brass</strong> players make sound by buzzing their lips into a mouthpiece. The family includes <strong>trumpet, horn, trombone, tuba</strong> from small to big.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Hit",
   "h2": "Percussion Splits",
   "body_html": "<p><strong>Percussion</strong> divides into <strong>tuned</strong> (xylophone, timpani — play notes) and <strong>untuned</strong> (snare, cymbal — no pitch). Anything you hit counts.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Slide",
   "h2": "Trombone's Trick",
   "body_html": "<p>The <strong>trombone</strong> is the only brass with a <strong>slide</strong> rather than valves. Pushing the slide out lengthens the tube and lowers the pitch.</p>"
  }
 ],
